# controls — reserved, deliberately empty

This directory is empty on purpose, and this file exists only because git tracks
files rather than directories. It is not an unfinished source file.

Nothing has been written here yet because of Δ2: appcraft does not author a control
library. Controls come from Astryx, and what eventually lands here is the thin
adaptation layer — binding Astryx components to the projection facade — not
primitives of our own. Authoring a novel primitive instead requires the
`custom-control-justified` escape hatch and stronger coverage.

Governed by the `controls` route (docs/routes.json). The boundary rules that apply
are enforced, not described: `boundaries/element-types` in eslint.config.js and the
matching rules in .dependency-cruiser.cjs. Read those for the real constraints — a
comment in this file could drift from them without anything noticing.

Delete this file once real source lands here.
